  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate and Ataxin-2 through a series of molecular interactions. Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate is identified as a target of two different compounds, 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide and Khrinone C, both of which are implicated in targeting Ataxin-2. The CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, a key enzyme in the sialylation pathway, serves as a common intermediate in these interactions. This enzyme is likely involved in the modification of proteins, including Ataxin-2, which is associated with ataxia and neurodegenerative processes. The evidence indicates that Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate may influence the activity of this enzyme, thereby affecting the downstream pathway that leads to Ataxin-2 modification. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct involvement of Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate in the regulation of Ataxin-2.",
